<http://www.spektrix.com/nacc/event/35601ALVJGKRTKBQLPHGRMJPNQQKSPRPT> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "The 2026 CBC Massey Lectures";
  schema:description """
	Under international human rights law, we’re all guaranteed the right to housing – not just a roof over our heads, but housing that is affordable and secure and which allows our inherent human dignity to flourish. But governments worldwide have failed to uphold that right. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>In the 2026 CBC Massey Lectures, Leilani Farha, global director of The Shift and former UN special rapporteur on the Right to Housing, reckons with a crisis engineered by governments and perfected by financial firms. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>In her Yellowknife Massey Lecture, called “The Very Human Right to Home,” she explores what it will take to make the right to housing real.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Join us for a discussion on housing and home in the Northwest Territories, moderated by CBC IDEAS host Nahlah Ayed. Which paths show the most promise in creating security for everyone, both in terms of physical housing and our relationship to the land?
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-10-01T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/nacc/files/52402156-2140-413b-b1f7-f13b5f161a4d.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/nacc/location/405AGDKDKNLGVLJCSNTLQBVTRTGBTHCPJ>;
  schema:url <https://naccnt.ca/events/the-2026-cbc-massey-lectures/>;
  schema:offers _:59e0d1189b9e4ff0a83f6dc3bf844c9a3834;
  schema:duration "PT150M";
  schema:endDate "2026-10-01T21:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

